/-!
# The Stein factorization of an alteration in the model

This file implements the blueprint nodes `def:gl-stein` and `lem:gl-stein`(1),(2) of `global.tex`
for the formalization of Fang–Han–Xia, *The envelope property for unibranch projective varieties*
(FHX, Step 1 of the proof of Theorem 6.1, `thm:normal-ample-EP`).

Let `X = V(I) ⊆ ℙ^N` and let `A : X.Alteration` be an alteration in model form
(`thm:gl-dejong`, `EnvelopeProperty.Global.DeJongImport`): a bihomogeneous prime
`I_Y ⊆ k[x, y]` with `I_Y ∩ k[x] = I`, `k(Y)` finite over `k(X)`, and smooth rank-2 quotient model
`𝒴 = (k(Y), S_Y, (x, y))` (`ProjSubvariety.Alteration.model`).

## The model `𝒳` of `X` inside `k(Y)` (`def:gl-stein`)

`k(X)` is the subfield `ProjSubvariety.Alteration.BaseField` of `k(Y)` generated by the ratios
`x̄_i / x̄_{i₀}` (`i₀ = A.xIndex`), and `𝒳 = (k(X), S_X, x)` (`Alteration.baseModel`) is the rank-1
model with `S_X = k[(x̄_i / x̄_{i₀}) T] ⊆ k(X)[T]`. Since `I_Y ∩ k[x] = I`, the presentation
`k[x_0, …, x_N] → S_X`, `x_i ↦ (x̄_i / x̄_{i₀}) T` (`Alteration.basePres`, a
`MultiModel.DegOnePres`) has kernel `I` (`Alteration.basePres_ideal`,
`Alteration.basePres_toProjSubvariety`): `𝒳` is the quotient model of `I`
(`rmk:gl-model-examples`(1)) with its function field realized inside `k(Y)`, so that
`S_X ⊆ k(Y)[T_1] ⊆ k(Y)[T_1, T_2]` literally. (The blueprint writes `𝒳 = 𝒳_I` with
`K = Frac(k[x]/I)_0`; the two are isomorphic, and the bridge lemmas of `rmk:gl-bridges` only use a
presentation in degree `1` with kernel `I`.)

## The Stein model `𝒯` (`def:gl-stein`, `lem:gl-stein`(1))

`𝒯 = (k(Y), S_T, x)` (`Alteration.steinModel`) is the normalization of `𝒳` in `k(Y)`
(`MultiModel.normalizationIn`): `S_T` is the integral closure of `S_X` in `k(Y)[T_1]`. It is a
normal model of rank `1` (`Alteration.isNormal_steinModel`) with function field `k(Y)` (by
construction), and `h : 𝒯 → 𝒳` (`Alteration.steinHom`, `MultiModel.FiniteHom.ofNormalizationIn`)
is a finite morphism of degree `[k(Y) : k(X)]` (the degree of a finite morphism is the degree of its
field extension, finite by `ProjSubvariety.Alteration.finiteDimensional`). Projective normality of
`X` is not needed for (1), (2) and (3).

## The map `β : 𝒴^an → 𝒯^an` (`lem:gl-stein`(2))

* `T ↦ T_1` is `MultiModel.firstFactorHom : K[T] → K[T_1, T_2]` (degrees `MultiModel.firstDeg`).
* `S_T ⊆ S_Y^ν` (`Alteration.firstFactorHom_mem_normalization`): an element of `S_T` is integral
  over `S_X ⊆ S_Y` (`Alteration.baseToModel_mem`).
* The chart algebras of `𝒴` are integrally closed (smoothness, `def:gl-smooth`), so restriction
  `𝒴^{ν,an} → 𝒴^an` is a homeomorphism (`lem:gl-model-change`,
  `MultiModel.FiniteHom.anHomeomorphOfSelf`; `Alteration.normHomeomorph`): every `y ∈ 𝒴^an` has a
  unique extension `ỹ` to `S_Y^ν`.
* `β(y) = ỹ|_{S_T}` (`Alteration.steinBeta`), continuous (`Alteration.continuous_steinBeta`), with
  `β(⋆) = ⋆` (`Alteration.steinBeta_triv`) and `h ∘ β` the restriction to `S_X`
  (`Alteration.steinHom_anMap_steinBeta`, `Alteration.baseAnMap`).
* Sections and psh functions (`lem:gl-stein`(2)): a section of degree `a` of `𝒯` is a section of
  degree `(a, 0)` of `𝒴` with `|f|_y = |f|_{β(y)}` (`Alteration.mem_sections_stein`,
  `Alteration.secAbs_steinBeta`); hence Fubini–Study functions of class `a` on `𝒯` pull back to
  Fubini–Study functions of class `(a, 0)` on `𝒴` (`Alteration.isFS_comp_steinBeta`), and
  `u ∘ β ∈ PSH(𝒴, (θ, 0))` for `u ∈ PSH(𝒯, θ)` (`Alteration.isPSH_comp_steinBeta`).

## `lem:gl-stein`(3): the blowup

For the data `ProjSubvariety.Alteration.SteinBlowup` (existence: `Alteration.nonempty_steinBlowup`):

* `e` and a presentation `P` in degree `1` of the Veronese `𝒯_(e)` (`lem:wu-veronese`,
  `MultiModel.exists_degOnePres_veronese`); `T' = V(I_{T'})` its `ProjSubvariety`, projectively
  normal since `𝒯` is normal (`Alteration.isProjNormal_steinTarget`), and
  `τ : 𝒯^an ≃ₜ T'^an` (`Alteration.steinTau`, Veronese homeomorphism and bridge), with
  `PSH(𝒯, e t) = PSH(T', t) ∘ τ` for `t ≥ 0` (`Alteration.isPSH_steinTau_iff`);
* the forms `G_m` (`Alteration.steinCenter`): `G_m(w) = (ȳ_m / ȳ_{m₀}) h` for some `0 ≠ h ∈ (S_T)_{eD}`
  (`Alteration.exists_steinCenterData`, a common denominator), so `ȳ_m / ȳ_{m₀} = G_m / G_{m₀}`;
* the model `𝒲 = (k(Y), k[w_i U_1, (ȳ_m / ȳ_{m₀}) U_2], (w, ȳ / ȳ_{m₀}))`
  (`Alteration.blowupModel`): the kernel of its presentation `k[x', y] → S_𝒲` is the ideal `I'` of
  the blowup `B` of `T'` along `(G_m)` (`Alteration.blowupModel_biIdeal`: for `F` of bidegree
  `(a, b)`, `F(x', G) = h^b F(w, ȳ / ȳ_{m₀})`, `lem:pg-blowup-basic`(1)), and
  `S_{(e,1)}(𝒴) ⊆ S_𝒲 ⊆ S_{(e,1)}(𝒴^ν)` with mutually integral coordinates
  (`Alteration.isModelChange_blowupModel`, `Alteration.isModelChange_blowupModel_normalization`);
  the elements of `S_𝒲` are sections of `𝒴_{(e,1)}` by the ideal argument on `𝒴`
  (`Alteration.hasSections_blowupModel`);
* `ϑ : 𝒴^an ≃ₜ 𝒴_{(e,1)}^an ≃ₜ 𝒲^an ≃ₜ B^an` (`Alteration.steinTheta`; the `(e, 1)`-Veronese is
  `MultiModel.biVeronese`, `EnvelopeProperty.Global.BiVeronese`), with
  `|q|_{ϑ_𝒲(y)} = |ψ(q)|_{ỹ}` (`Alteration.blowupHomeomorph_val`), hence `μ ∘ ϑ = τ ∘ β`
  (`Alteration.proj_steinTheta`), and `PSH(𝒴, (e t, s)) = PSH(B, (t, s)) ∘ ϑ` for `t, s ≥ 0`
  (`Alteration.isPSH_steinTheta_iff`; `lem:gl-veronese` with the rescaling `(e, 1)`,
  `lem:gl-model-change`, `lem:gl-bridge-psh`(2)).
* `β` is surjective (`Alteration.steinBeta_surjective`): `β = τ⁻¹ ∘ μ ∘ ϑ` and `μ` is surjective
  (`lem:pg-blowup-surjective`).

The psh correspondences are stated for `t, s ≥ 0` (the bridges `lem:gl-bridge-psh` hold for
nonnegative classes); FHX use `t = 1/e`, `s = 0`. For a projectively normal `X`,
`Alteration.isNormal_baseModel` and `Alteration.hasEnvelopeProperty_iff_baseModel` connect `𝒳`
with `X`.
-/

open scoped NNReal ENNReal Topology

open Topology Filter MvPolynomial

noncomputable section

namespace EnvelopeProperty

universe u

namespace MultiModel

/-! ### The inclusion `K[T] → K[T_1, T_2]` of the first factor -/

section FirstFactor

variable {k : Type u} [Field k] {K : Type u} [Field K] [Algebra k K]

theorem injective_const_zero_fin_one : Function.Injective fun _ : Fin 1 => (0 : Fin 2) :=
  fun a b _ => Subsingleton.elim a b

variable (k K) in
/-- The inclusion `K[T] → K[T_1, T_2]`, `T ↦ T_1` (the first factor of `ℙ^N × ℙ^{N'}`; the
variables are indexed from `0`). -/
def firstFactorHom : MvPolynomial (Fin 1) K →ₐ[k] MvPolynomial (Fin 2) K :=
  (rename fun _ : Fin 1 => (0 : Fin 2)).restrictScalars k

/-- The degree `(a, 0) ∈ ℕ^2` of `T_1^a`. -/
def firstDeg (a : Fin 1 →₀ ℕ) : Fin 2 →₀ ℕ :=
  Finsupp.mapDomain (fun _ : Fin 1 => (0 : Fin 2)) a

theorem firstDeg_add (a b : Fin 1 →₀ ℕ) : firstDeg (a + b) = firstDeg a + firstDeg b :=
  Finsupp.mapDomain_add

theorem firstDeg_zero : firstDeg 0 = 0 :=
  Finsupp.mapDomain_zero

theorem firstDeg_single (c : Fin 1) (n : ℕ) : firstDeg (Finsupp.single c n) = Finsupp.single 0 n :=
  Finsupp.mapDomain_single

theorem firstDeg_injective : Function.Injective firstDeg :=
  Finsupp.mapDomain_injective injective_const_zero_fin_one

theorem firstDeg_apply_zero (a : Fin 1 →₀ ℕ) : firstDeg a 0 = a 0 := by
  rw [fin_one_eq_single a, firstDeg_single, Finsupp.single_eq_same, Finsupp.single_eq_same]

theorem firstDeg_apply_of_ne_zero (a : Fin 1 →₀ ℕ) {c : Fin 2} (hc : c ≠ 0) : firstDeg a c = 0 := by
  rw [fin_one_eq_single a, firstDeg_single, Finsupp.single_eq_of_ne hc]

theorem firstDeg_apply_one (a : Fin 1 →₀ ℕ) : firstDeg a 1 = 0 :=
  firstDeg_apply_of_ne_zero a (by decide)

theorem firstFactorHom_monomial (a : Fin 1 →₀ ℕ) (f : K) :
    firstFactorHom k K (monomial a f) = monomial (firstDeg a) f :=
  rename_monomial _ _ _

theorem firstFactorHom_injective : Function.Injective (firstFactorHom k K) :=
  rename_injective _ injective_const_zero_fin_one

theorem coeff_firstFactorHom (p : MvPolynomial (Fin 1) K) (a : Fin 1 →₀ ℕ) :
    (firstFactorHom k K p).coeff (firstDeg a) = p.coeff a :=
  coeff_rename_mapDomain _ injective_const_zero_fin_one _ _

/-- `T ↦ T_1` maps the homogeneous component of degree `a` to that of degree `(a, 0)`. -/
theorem firstFactorHom_monomial_coeff (p : MvPolynomial (Fin 1) K) (a : Fin 1 →₀ ℕ) :
    firstFactorHom k K (monomial a (p.coeff a)) =
      monomial (firstDeg a) ((firstFactorHom k K p).coeff (firstDeg a)) := by
  rw [firstFactorHom_monomial, coeff_firstFactorHom]

/-- The degree `(a, 0) ∈ ℤ^2` of a degree `a ∈ ℤ^1`. -/
def steinDeg {α : Type*} [Zero α] (a : Fin 1 → α) : Fin 2 → α :=
  ![a 0, 0]

@[simp]
theorem steinDeg_zero {α : Type*} [Zero α] (a : Fin 1 → α) : steinDeg a 0 = a 0 :=
  rfl

@[simp]
theorem steinDeg_one {α : Type*} [Zero α] (a : Fin 1 → α) : steinDeg a 1 = 0 :=
  rfl

theorem addDeg_steinDeg (a : Fin 1 → ℤ) (b : Fin 1 →₀ ℕ) :
    addDeg (steinDeg a) (firstDeg b) = firstDeg (addDeg a b) := by
  ext c
  fin_cases c
  · change (steinDeg a 0 + (firstDeg b 0 : ℤ)).toNat = firstDeg (addDeg a b) 0
    rw [firstDeg_apply_zero, firstDeg_apply_zero, steinDeg_zero, addDeg_apply]
  · change (steinDeg a 1 + (firstDeg b 1 : ℤ)).toNat = firstDeg (addDeg a b) 1
    rw [firstDeg_apply_one, firstDeg_apply_one, steinDeg_one]
    rfl

end FirstFactor

/-- Under `x_i ↦ c_i T^{τ(w_i)}`, a polynomial of weight `γ` maps to `F(c) T^{τ(γ)}`. -/
theorem aeval_monomial_family_of_isWeightedHomogeneous {k : Type u} [Field k] {K : Type u}
    [Field K] [Algebra k K] {σ ι Γ : Type*} [AddCommMonoid Γ] (τ : Γ →+ (ι →₀ ℕ)) (w : σ → Γ)
    (c : σ → K) {γ : Γ} {F : MvPolynomial σ k} (hF : F.IsWeightedHomogeneous w γ) :
    aeval (fun i => (monomial (τ (w i)) (c i) : MvPolynomial ι K)) F = monomial (τ γ) (aeval c F) := by
  induction hF using IsWeightedHomogeneous.induction_on with
  | zero => simp
  | add p q hp hq ihp ihq => rw [map_add, map_add, ihp, ihq, map_add]
  | monomial e r hr => rw [aeval_monomial_family, hr, aeval_monomial]

end MultiModel

namespace ProjSubvariety.Alteration

open MultiModel

variable {k : Type u} [Field k] {N : ℕ} {X : ProjSubvariety k N} (A : X.Alteration)

/-! ### The function field `k(X) ⊆ k(Y)` and the model `𝒳` -/

/-- The function field `k(X)`, realized as the subfield of `k(Y)` generated by the ratios
`x̄_i / x̄_{i₀}` (`I_Y ∩ k[x] = I`). -/
abbrev BaseField : Type u :=
  quotBlockField A.ideal A.index 0

/-- `k(Y)` is finite over `k(X)`. -/
instance finiteDimensional_baseField : FiniteDimensional A.BaseField A.FunField :=
  A.finiteDimensional

/-- The coordinates `x̄_i / x̄_{i₀} ∈ k(X)` of `𝒳`. -/
def baseCoord (_ : Fin 1) (i : Fin (N + 1)) : A.BaseField :=
  ⟨quotCoord A.ideal A.index 0 i, quotCoord_mem_quotBlockField _ _ _ _⟩

@[simp]
theorem coe_baseCoord (c : Fin 1) (i : Fin (N + 1)) :
    (A.baseCoord c i : A.FunField) = quotCoord A.ideal A.index 0 i :=
  rfl

theorem algebraMap_baseCoord (c : Fin 1) (i : Fin (N + 1)) :
    algebraMap A.BaseField A.FunField (A.baseCoord c i) = quotCoord A.ideal A.index 0 i :=
  rfl

theorem baseCoord_xIndex (c : Fin 1) : A.baseCoord c A.xIndex = 1 :=
  Subtype.ext (quotCoord_self A.index A.isRelevantAt 0)

/-- The coordinate ring `S_X = k[(x̄_i / x̄_{i₀}) T] ⊆ k(X)[T]` of `𝒳`. -/
def baseS : Subalgebra k (MvPolynomial (Fin 1) A.BaseField) :=
  Algebra.adjoin k (Set.range fun i : (Σ _ : Fin 1, Fin (N + 1)) =>
    monomial (Finsupp.single i.1 1) (A.baseCoord i.1 i.2))

/-- **The model `𝒳` of `X = V(I)`** (`def:gl-stein`; `rmk:gl-model-examples`(1) with the
function field realized inside `k(Y)`): `(k(X), S_X, x)`, `S_X = k[(x̄_i / x̄_{i₀}) T]`. -/
def baseModel : MultiModel k A.BaseField 1 where
  S := A.baseS
  isGraded _ hp a := monomial_coeff_mem_adjoin (fun q hq => by
    obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := hq
    exact ⟨_, _, rfl⟩) hp a
  fg := ⟨(Set.finite_range _).toFinset, by rw [Set.Finite.coe_toFinset]; rfl⟩
  M := fun _ => N
  coord := A.baseCoord
  coord_mem c j := Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨⟨c, j⟩, rfl⟩
  exists_coord_ne_zero c := ⟨A.xIndex, by rw [baseCoord_xIndex]; exact one_ne_zero⟩
  isIntegral p hp := isIntegral_algebraMap (R := A.baseS) (x := ⟨p, hp⟩)
  generates := by
    rw [eq_top_iff]
    rintro x -
    set s := {x : A.BaseField | ∃ (a : Fin 1 →₀ ℕ) (f g : A.BaseField),
      monomial a f ∈ A.baseS ∧ monomial a g ∈ A.baseS ∧ g ≠ 0 ∧ x = f / g} with hs
    have hgen : ∀ i : Fin (N + 1), A.baseCoord 0 i ∈ s := fun i =>
      ⟨Finsupp.single 0 1, A.baseCoord 0 i, A.baseCoord 0 A.xIndex,
        Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨⟨0, i⟩, rfl⟩, Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨⟨0, A.xIndex⟩, rfl⟩,
        by rw [baseCoord_xIndex]; exact one_ne_zero, by rw [baseCoord_xIndex, div_one]⟩
    have hle : quotBlockField A.ideal A.index 0 ≤
        (IntermediateField.adjoin k s).map (quotBlockField A.ideal A.index 0).val := by
      change IntermediateField.adjoin k (Set.range (quotCoord A.ideal A.index 0)) ≤ _
      rw [IntermediateField.adjoin_le_iff]
      rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
      exact (IntermediateField.mem_map _).2 ⟨A.baseCoord 0 i,
        IntermediateField.subset_adjoin _ _ (hgen i), rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨y, hy, hyx⟩ := (IntermediateField.mem_map _).1 (hle x.2)
    rwa [Subtype.val_injective hyx] at hy

theorem baseModel_S : A.baseModel.S = A.baseS :=
  rfl

theorem baseModel_coord : A.baseModel.coord = A.baseCoord :=
  rfl

theorem baseModel_M : A.baseModel.M = fun _ => N :=
  rfl

/-- `S_X` is generated by its coordinates. -/
theorem baseModel_S_eq_coordAlg : A.baseModel.S = A.baseModel.coordAlg :=
  rfl

/-- **The presentation of `𝒳` in degree `1`**: `x_i ↦ (x̄_i / x̄_{i₀}) T` (`rmk:gl-bridges`). -/
def basePres : DegOnePres A.baseModel N where
  w := A.baseCoord 0
  mem i := A.baseModel.coord_mem_piece 0 i
  adjoin_eq := by
    change Algebra.adjoin k _ = A.baseS
    refine congrArg (Algebra.adjoin k) (Set.ext fun p => ⟨?_, ?_⟩)
    · rintro ⟨i, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨⟨0, i⟩, rfl⟩
    · rintro ⟨⟨c, i⟩, rfl⟩
      obtain rfl := Fin.fin_one_eq_zero c
      exact ⟨i, rfl⟩

/-! ### `S_X ⊆ S_Y` -/

section BaseToModel

/-- The map `k(X)[T] → k(Y)[T_1, T_2]`, `f T^a ↦ f T_1^a`. -/
def baseToModel : MvPolynomial (Fin 1) A.BaseField →ₐ[k] MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A.FunField :=
  (firstFactorHom k A.FunField).comp (coeffMap k A.FunField)

theorem baseToModel_monomial (a : Fin 1 →₀ ℕ) (f : A.BaseField) :
    A.baseToModel (monomial a f) = monomial (firstDeg a) (f : A.FunField) := by
  rw [baseToModel, AlgHom.comp_apply, coeffMap_monomial, firstFactorHom_monomial]
  rfl

theorem baseToModel_injective : Function.Injective A.baseToModel :=
  (firstFactorHom_injective (k := k) (K := A.FunField)).comp (coeffMap_injective (K := A.BaseField) (r := 1) (k := k) A.FunField)

/-- The generators of `S_X` map to the `x`-coordinates of `𝒴`. -/
theorem baseToModel_gen (c : Fin 1) (i : Fin (N + 1)) :
    A.baseToModel (monomial (Finsupp.single c 1) (A.baseCoord c i)) =
      quotGen A.ideal A.index ⟨0, i⟩ := by
  rw [baseToModel_monomial, firstDeg_single]
  rfl

/-- **`S_X ⊆ S_Y`**: `f T^a ↦ f T_1^a` maps `S_X` into `S_Y`. -/
theorem baseToModel_mem {p : MvPolynomial (Fin 1) A.BaseField} (hp : p ∈ A.baseModel.S) :
    A.baseToModel p ∈ A.model.S := by
  have h : A.baseModel.S.map A.baseToModel ≤ A.model.S := by
    change A.baseS.map A.baseToModel ≤ _
    rw [baseS, AlgHom.map_adjoin, Algebra.adjoin_le_iff]
    rintro _ ⟨_, ⟨⟨c, i⟩, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    rw [baseToModel_gen]
    exact Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨⟨0, i⟩, rfl⟩
  exact h ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩

/-- The inclusion `S_X → S_Y`. -/
def baseRingHom : A.baseModel.S →ₐ[k] A.model.S :=
  (A.baseToModel.comp A.baseModel.S.val).codRestrict _ fun p => A.baseToModel_mem p.2

@[simp]
theorem coe_baseRingHom (p : A.baseModel.S) :
    (A.baseRingHom p : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A.FunField) = A.baseToModel p.1 :=
  rfl

theorem baseRingHom_injective : Function.Injective A.baseRingHom := fun _ _ h =>
  Subtype.ext (A.baseToModel_injective (congrArg Subtype.val h))

theorem baseRingHom_homComp (a : Fin 1 →₀ ℕ) (p : A.baseModel.S) :
    A.baseRingHom (A.baseModel.homComp a p) = A.model.homComp (firstDeg a) (A.baseRingHom p) := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  rw [coe_baseRingHom, coe_homComp, coe_homComp, coe_baseRingHom, baseToModel_monomial,
    baseToModel, AlgHom.comp_apply, coeff_firstFactorHom, coeffMap_apply, coeff_map]
  rfl

theorem baseRingHom_coordElem (j : Fin (N + 1)) :
    A.baseRingHom (A.baseModel.coordElem ⟨0, j⟩) = A.model.coordElem ⟨0, j⟩ := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  rw [coe_baseRingHom, coe_coordElem, coe_coordElem]
  exact A.baseToModel_gen 0 j

end BaseToModel

/-! ### The kernel of the presentation of `𝒳` -/

/-- The composite `k[x] → S_X → k(Y)[T_1, T_2]` is `x_i ↦ z^{(0)}_i`, the presentation of `𝒴`
restricted to `k[x]`. -/
theorem baseToModel_comp_hom :
    A.baseToModel.comp A.basePres.hom = (quotMap A.ideal A.index).comp (alterationIncl N A.N') := by
  refine MvPolynomial.algHom_ext fun i => ?_
  rw [AlgHom.comp_apply, AlgHom.comp_apply, DegOnePres.hom_X, alterationIncl, rename_X,
    quotMap_X]
  exact A.baseToModel_gen 0 i

/-- **The kernel of the presentation of `𝒳` is `I`** (`I_Y ∩ k[x] = I`, `ker(k[x, y] → S_Y) =
I_Y` by `MultiModel.ker_quotMap`). -/
theorem basePres_ideal : A.basePres.ideal = X.ideal := by
  ext F
  rw [DegOnePres.mem_ideal_iff, ← A.comap_eq, Ideal.mem_comap,
    ← (Ideal.ext_iff.1 (ker_quotMap A.isRelevantAt A.isMultihomogeneous)) _, RingHom.mem_ker]
  constructor
  · intro h
    have := congrArg A.baseToModel h
    rwa [map_zero, ← AlgHom.comp_apply, baseToModel_comp_hom, AlgHom.comp_apply] at this
  · intro h
    apply A.baseToModel_injective
    rw [map_zero, ← AlgHom.comp_apply, baseToModel_comp_hom, AlgHom.comp_apply]
    exact h

/-- **The presentation of `𝒳` is the given `X = V(I) ⊆ ℙ^N`.** -/
theorem basePres_toProjSubvariety : A.basePres.toProjSubvariety = X := by
  have h : A.basePres.toProjSubvariety.ideal = X.ideal := A.basePres_ideal
  generalize A.basePres.toProjSubvariety = Z at h
  cases Z
  cases X
  congr

/-! ### Restriction to `S_X` -/

/-- The restriction `𝒴^an → 𝒳^an` along `S_X ⊆ S_Y` (`y ↦ y|_{S_X}`). -/
def baseAnMap (y : A.model.an) : A.baseModel.an :=
  ⟨Berk.comap A.baseRingHom y.1, fun p a => by
    rw [Berk.comap_val_apply, Berk.comap_val_apply, baseRingHom_homComp]
    exact y.2.1 _ _, fun c => by
    obtain rfl := Fin.fin_one_eq_zero c
    refine (Finset.sup_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_).trans (y.2.2 0)
    rw [Berk.comap_val_apply]
    exact congrArg y.1.val (A.baseRingHom_coordElem j)⟩

theorem baseAnMap_val (y : A.model.an) (p : A.baseModel.S) :
    (A.baseAnMap y).1.val p = y.1.val (A.baseRingHom p) :=
  rfl

theorem continuous_baseAnMap : Continuous A.baseAnMap :=
  A.baseModel.continuous_iff_an.2 fun p =>
    (Berk.continuous_val_apply (A.baseRingHom p)).comp continuous_subtype_val

/-- The chart algebras of the smooth `𝒴` are integrally closed (`def:gl-smooth`). -/
theorem isIntegrallyClosed_chartAlg_model :
    ∀ j : A.model.ChartIndex, (∀ c, A.model.coord c (j c) ≠ 0) →
      IsIntegrallyClosed (A.model.chartAlg j) :=
  fun _ hj => A.isSmooth.isIntegrallyClosed hj

/-- If `X` is projectively normal, the model `𝒳` is normal (`lem:gl-bridge-psh`(1)). -/
theorem isNormal_baseModel (hX : X.IsProjNormal) : A.baseModel.IsNormal :=
  A.basePres.isProjNormal_toProjSubvariety_iff.1 (by rw [A.basePres_toProjSubvariety]; exact hX)

/-- **`EP_X(t) ↔ EP_𝒳(t)`** for `t ≥ 0` and `X` projectively normal (`lem:gl-bridge-psh`(1) for
the presentation `basePres` of `𝒳`, whose kernel is `I`). -/
theorem hasEnvelopeProperty_iff_baseModel (hX : X.IsProjNormal) {t : ℝ} (ht : 0 ≤ t) :
    X.HasEnvelopeProperty t ↔ A.baseModel.HasEnvelopeProperty fun _ => t := by
  have h := A.basePres.hasEnvelopeProperty_toProjSubvariety_iff
    (by rw [A.basePres_toProjSubvariety]; exact hX) ht
  rw [A.basePres_toProjSubvariety] at h
  exact h

/-! ### The Stein model `𝒯` (`def:gl-stein`, `lem:gl-stein`(1)) -/

section Stein

variable [IsAlgClosed k]

/-- **The Stein model** `𝒯 = (k(Y), S_T, x)` (`def:gl-stein`): `S_T` is the integral closure of
`S_X` in `k(Y)[T]` (the normalization of `𝒳` in `k(Y)`, `rmk:gl-model-examples`(3)). -/
def steinModel : MultiModel k A.FunField 1 :=
  A.baseModel.normalizationIn A.FunField

/-- **The finite morphism `h : 𝒯 → 𝒳`** (`def:gl-stein`, `lem:gl-stein`(1)), of degree
`[k(Y) : k(X)]`. -/
def steinHom : FiniteHom A.steinModel A.baseModel :=
  FiniteHom.ofNormalizationIn (E := A.FunField) A.baseModel

/-- **`𝒯` is normal** (`lem:gl-stein`(1)). -/
theorem isNormal_steinModel : A.steinModel.IsNormal :=
  A.baseModel.isNormal_normalizationIn (E := A.FunField)

theorem mem_steinModel_S {p : MvPolynomial (Fin 1) A.FunField} :
    p ∈ A.steinModel.S ↔ IsIntegral (A.baseModel.imageS A.FunField) p :=
  Iff.rfl

theorem steinModel_M : A.steinModel.M = fun _ => N :=
  rfl

theorem steinModel_coord (c : Fin 1) (i : Fin (N + 1)) :
    A.steinModel.coord c i = quotCoord A.ideal A.index 0 i :=
  rfl

/-- **`S_T ⊆ S_Y^ν`** (`lem:gl-stein`(2)): elements of `S_T` are integral over `S_X ⊆ S_Y`. -/
theorem firstFactorHom_mem_normalization {p : MvPolynomial (Fin 1) A.FunField}
    (hp : p ∈ A.steinModel.S) : firstFactorHom k A.FunField p ∈ A.model.normalization.S := by
  rw [mem_normalization_S]
  have hmem : ∀ q ∈ A.baseModel.imageS A.FunField, firstFactorHom k A.FunField q ∈ A.model.S := by
    rintro _ ⟨q, hq, rfl⟩
    exact A.baseToModel_mem hq
  let φ : A.baseModel.imageS A.FunField →+* A.model.S :=
    ((firstFactorHom k A.FunField).toRingHom.comp
      (A.baseModel.imageS A.FunField).val.toRingHom).codRestrict A.model.S fun q => hmem q.1 q.2
  exact IsIntegral.map_of_comp_eq φ (firstFactorHom k A.FunField).toRingHom
    (RingHom.ext fun _ => rfl) (A.mem_steinModel_S.1 hp)

/-- The inclusion `S_T → S_Y^ν`. -/
def steinRingHom : A.steinModel.S →ₐ[k] A.model.normalization.S :=
  ((firstFactorHom k A.FunField).comp A.steinModel.S.val).codRestrict _ fun p =>
    A.firstFactorHom_mem_normalization p.2

@[simp]
theorem coe_steinRingHom (p : A.steinModel.S) :
    (A.steinRingHom p : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A.FunField) = firstFactorHom k A.FunField p.1 :=
  rfl

theorem steinRingHom_injective : Function.Injective A.steinRingHom := fun _ _ h =>
  Subtype.ext (firstFactorHom_injective (k := k) (K := A.FunField) (congrArg Subtype.val h))

theorem steinRingHom_homComp (a : Fin 1 →₀ ℕ) (p : A.steinModel.S) :
    A.steinRingHom (A.steinModel.homComp a p) =
      A.model.normalization.homComp (firstDeg a) (A.steinRingHom p) := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  rw [coe_steinRingHom, coe_homComp, coe_homComp, coe_steinRingHom,
    firstFactorHom_monomial_coeff]

theorem steinRingHom_coordElem (j : Fin (N + 1)) :
    A.steinRingHom (A.steinModel.coordElem ⟨0, j⟩) = A.model.normalization.coordElem ⟨0, j⟩ := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  rw [coe_steinRingHom, coe_coordElem, coe_coordElem, firstFactorHom_monomial, firstDeg_single]
  rfl

/-- `S_X → S_T → S_Y^ν` is `S_X → S_Y → S_Y^ν`. -/
theorem steinRingHom_algHom (p : A.baseModel.S) :
    A.steinRingHom (A.steinHom.algHom p) =
      (FiniteHom.ofNormalization A.model).algHom (A.baseRingHom p) := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  rw [coe_steinRingHom, FiniteHom.coe_algHom, FiniteHom.coe_algHom, FiniteHom.coeffMap_self,
    coe_baseRingHom]
  rfl

/-! ### The map `β : 𝒴^an → 𝒯^an` (`lem:gl-stein`(2)) -/

/-- **The unique extension to `S_Y^ν`** (`lem:gl-model-change`): restriction
`𝒴^{ν,an} → 𝒴^an` is a homeomorphism, since the chart algebras of `𝒴` are integrally closed. -/
def normHomeomorph : A.model.normalization.an ≃ₜ A.model.an :=
  (FiniteHom.ofNormalization A.model).anHomeomorphOfSelf A.isIntegrallyClosed_chartAlg_model

theorem normHomeomorph_apply (w : A.model.normalization.an) :
    A.normHomeomorph w = (FiniteHom.ofNormalization A.model).anMap w :=
  rfl

theorem normHomeomorph_triv : A.normHomeomorph A.model.normalization.triv = A.model.triv :=
  (FiniteHom.ofNormalization A.model).anMap_triv

/-- The restriction `𝒴^{ν,an} → 𝒯^an` along `S_T ⊆ S_Y^ν`. -/
def steinAnMap (w : A.model.normalization.an) : A.steinModel.an :=
  ⟨Berk.comap A.steinRingHom w.1, fun p a => by
    rw [Berk.comap_val_apply, Berk.comap_val_apply, steinRingHom_homComp]
    exact w.2.1 _ _, fun c => by
    obtain rfl := Fin.fin_one_eq_zero c
    refine (Finset.sup_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_).trans (w.2.2 0)
    rw [Berk.comap_val_apply]
    exact congrArg w.1.val (A.steinRingHom_coordElem j)⟩

theorem steinAnMap_val (w : A.model.normalization.an) (p : A.steinModel.S) :
    (A.steinAnMap w).1.val p = w.1.val (A.steinRingHom p) :=
  rfl

theorem continuous_steinAnMap : Continuous A.steinAnMap :=
  A.steinModel.continuous_iff_an.2 fun p =>
    (Berk.continuous_val_apply (A.steinRingHom p)).comp continuous_subtype_val

theorem steinAnMap_triv : A.steinAnMap A.model.normalization.triv = A.steinModel.triv := by
  classical
  refine Subtype.ext (Berk.ext_val fun p => ?_)
  rw [steinAnMap_val]
  by_cases hp : p = 0
  · rw [hp, map_zero, map_zero, map_zero]
  · rw [A.steinModel.triv_val_of_ne_zero hp, A.model.normalization.triv_val_of_ne_zero fun h0 =>
      hp (A.steinRingHom_injective (h0.trans (map_zero _).symm))]

/-- **The map `β : 𝒴^an → 𝒯^an`** (`lem:gl-stein`(2)): `β(y) = ỹ|_{S_T}`, where `ỹ` is the unique
extension of `y` to `S_Y^ν`. -/
def steinBeta (y : A.model.an) : A.steinModel.an :=
  A.steinAnMap (A.normHomeomorph.symm y)

theorem steinBeta_val (y : A.model.an) (p : A.steinModel.S) :
    (A.steinBeta y).1.val p = (A.normHomeomorph.symm y).1.val (A.steinRingHom p) :=
  rfl

theorem continuous_steinBeta : Continuous A.steinBeta :=
  A.continuous_steinAnMap.comp A.normHomeomorph.symm.continuous

theorem steinBeta_triv : A.steinBeta A.model.triv = A.steinModel.triv := by
  rw [steinBeta, ← A.normHomeomorph_triv, Homeomorph.symm_apply_apply, steinAnMap_triv]

/-- **`h ∘ β` is the restriction to `S_X`** (`lem:gl-stein`(2)). -/
theorem steinHom_anMap_steinBeta (y : A.model.an) :
    A.steinHom.anMap (A.steinBeta y) = A.baseAnMap y := by
  refine Subtype.ext (Berk.ext_val fun p => ?_)
  have hy : y = (FiniteHom.ofNormalization A.model).anMap (A.normHomeomorph.symm y) := by
    rw [← normHomeomorph_apply, Homeomorph.apply_symm_apply]
  rw [FiniteHom.anMap_val, steinBeta_val, baseAnMap_val, steinRingHom_algHom]
  conv_rhs => rw [hy]
  rfl

theorem steinHom_anMap_comp_steinBeta : A.steinHom.anMap ∘ A.steinBeta = A.baseAnMap :=
  funext A.steinHom_anMap_steinBeta

/-! ### Multi-indices -/

/-- The coordinate indices of `𝒯` as coordinate indices of `𝒴` (the `x`-coordinates). -/
def steinCoordIndex (i : A.steinModel.CoordIndex) : A.model.CoordIndex :=
  ⟨0, i.2⟩

theorem steinCoordIndex_injective : Function.Injective A.steinCoordIndex := by
  rintro ⟨c, i⟩ ⟨c', i'⟩ h
  obtain rfl := Fin.fin_one_eq_zero c
  obtain rfl := Fin.fin_one_eq_zero c'
  have h' : i = i' := eq_of_heq (Sigma.mk.inj_iff.1 h).2
  rw [h']

/-- The multi-index of `𝒴` of a multi-index of `𝒯`. -/
def steinMon (γ : A.steinModel.CoordIndex →₀ ℕ) : A.model.CoordIndex →₀ ℕ :=
  Finsupp.mapDomain A.steinCoordIndex γ

theorem zCoeff_steinMon (γ : A.steinModel.CoordIndex →₀ ℕ) :
    A.model.zCoeff (A.steinMon γ) = A.steinModel.zCoeff γ := by
  rw [steinMon, zCoeff, zCoeff, Finsupp.prod_mapDomain_index (fun _ => pow_zero _)
    (fun _ _ _ => pow_add _ _ _)]
  rfl

theorem monDeg_steinMon (γ : A.steinModel.CoordIndex →₀ ℕ) :
    A.model.monDeg (A.steinMon γ) = firstDeg (A.steinModel.monDeg γ) := by
  rw [monDeg, monDeg, steinMon, firstDeg, ← Finsupp.mapDomain_comp, ← Finsupp.mapDomain_comp]
  rfl

theorem steinMon_mem_monSet {b : Fin 1 →₀ ℕ} {γ : A.steinModel.CoordIndex →₀ ℕ}
    (hγ : γ ∈ A.steinModel.monSet b) : A.steinMon γ ∈ A.model.monSet (firstDeg b) := by
  rw [mem_monSet, monDeg_steinMon, (mem_monSet _).1 hγ]

/-- Every multi-index of `𝒴` of degree `(b, 0)` comes from `𝒯`. -/
theorem exists_steinMon_eq {b : Fin 1 →₀ ℕ} {δ : A.model.CoordIndex →₀ ℕ}
    (hδ : δ ∈ A.model.monSet (firstDeg b)) :
    ∃ γ ∈ A.steinModel.monSet b, A.steinMon γ = δ := by
  classical
  have hδ' := (mem_monSet _).1 hδ
  -- `δ` vanishes on the `y`-coordinates.
  have hy : ∀ c : Fin 2, c ≠ 0 → ∀ m : Fin (A.model.M c + 1), δ ⟨c, m⟩ = 0 := by
    intro c hc m
    have h1 := congrArg (fun d : Fin 2 →₀ ℕ => d c) hδ'
    simp only [firstDeg_apply_of_ne_zero b hc] at h1
    rw [monDeg_apply] at h1
    exact (Finset.sum_eq_zero_iff.1 h1) m (Finset.mem_univ _)
  set γ : A.steinModel.CoordIndex →₀ ℕ :=
    Finsupp.equivFunOnFinite.symm fun i => δ (A.steinCoordIndex i)
  have hγδ : A.steinMon γ = δ := by
    ext ⟨c, j⟩
    by_cases hc : c = 0
    · subst hc
      rw [show (⟨0, j⟩ : A.model.CoordIndex) = A.steinCoordIndex ⟨0, j⟩ from rfl, steinMon,
        Finsupp.mapDomain_apply A.steinCoordIndex_injective]
      rfl
    · rw [steinMon, Finsupp.mapDomain_of_notMem_range]
      · exact (hy c hc j).symm
      · rintro ⟨⟨c', j'⟩, h⟩
        exact hc (congrArg Sigma.fst h).symm
  refine ⟨γ, (mem_monSet _).2 (firstDeg_injective ?_), hγδ⟩
  rw [← monDeg_steinMon, hγδ, hδ']

/-- `max_{δ ∈ Mon_𝒴(b, 0)} g(δ) = max_{γ ∈ Mon_𝒯(b)} g(γ)`. -/
theorem sup_monSet_steinMon (b : Fin 1 →₀ ℕ) (g : (A.model.CoordIndex →₀ ℕ) → ℝ≥0) :
    (A.model.monSet (firstDeg b)).sup g =
      (A.steinModel.monSet b).sup fun γ => g (A.steinMon γ) := by
  classical
  change _ = (A.steinModel.monSet b).sup (g ∘ A.steinMon)
  rw [← Finset.sup_image]
  congr 1
  ext δ
  rw [Finset.mem_image]
  exact ⟨fun h => A.exists_steinMon_eq h, fun ⟨γ, hγ, h⟩ => h ▸ A.steinMon_mem_monSet hγ⟩

/-! ### Sections and psh functions (`lem:gl-stein`(2)) -/

/-- Admissible degrees of `𝒯` give admissible degrees `(b, 0)` of `𝒴^ν`. -/
theorem isAdmissible_normalization {a : Fin 1 → ℤ} {b : Fin 1 →₀ ℕ} {f : A.FunField}
    (hf : A.steinModel.IsAdmissible a b f) :
    A.model.normalization.IsAdmissible (steinDeg a) (firstDeg b) f := by
  refine ⟨fun c => ?_, fun δ hδ => ?_⟩
  · fin_cases c
    · change 0 ≤ steinDeg a 0 + (firstDeg b 0 : ℤ)
      rw [steinDeg_zero, firstDeg_apply_zero]
      exact hf.nonneg 0
    · change 0 ≤ steinDeg a 1 + (firstDeg b 1 : ℤ)
      rw [steinDeg_one, firstDeg_apply_one]
      exact le_refl _
  · obtain ⟨γ, hγ, rfl⟩ := A.exists_steinMon_eq (b := b) hδ
    have h := hf.mul_zCoeff_mem hγ
    change monomial (addDeg (steinDeg a) (firstDeg b)) (f * A.model.zCoeff (A.steinMon γ)) ∈
      A.model.normalization.S
    rw [zCoeff_steinMon, addDeg_steinDeg, ← firstFactorHom_monomial (k := k)]
    exact A.firstFactorHom_mem_normalization h

/-- **Sections of `𝒯` are sections of `𝒴`** (`lem:gl-stein`(2)): `R_a(𝒯) ⊆ R_{(a, 0)}(𝒴)`. -/
theorem mem_sections_stein {a : Fin 1 → ℤ} {f : A.FunField} (hf : f ∈ A.steinModel.sections a) :
    f ∈ A.model.sections (steinDeg a) := by
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := hf
  rw [← (FiniteHom.ofNormalization A.model).sections_eq_of_self
    A.isIntegrallyClosed_chartAlg_model]
  exact (A.isAdmissible_normalization hb).mem_sections

/-- `|g|_{β(y)} = |g|_{ỹ}` for homogeneous `g T^d ∈ S_T`. -/
theorem homNorm_steinBeta (y : A.model.an) {d : Fin 1 →₀ ℕ} {g : A.FunField}
    (hg : g ∈ A.steinModel.piece d) :
    A.steinModel.homNorm (A.steinBeta y).1 d g =
      A.model.normalization.homNorm (A.normHomeomorph.symm y).1 (firstDeg d) g := by
  have hg' : g ∈ A.model.normalization.piece (firstDeg d) := by
    change monomial (firstDeg d) g ∈ A.model.normalization.S
    rw [← firstFactorHom_monomial (k := k)]
    exact A.firstFactorHom_mem_normalization hg
  rw [A.steinModel.homNorm_of_mem _ hg, A.model.normalization.homNorm_of_mem _ hg', steinBeta_val]
  refine congrArg (A.normHomeomorph.symm y).1.val (Subtype.ext ?_)
  rw [coe_steinRingHom, coe_ofPiece, coe_ofPiece, firstFactorHom_monomial]

/-- **Values of sections** (`lem:gl-stein`(2)): `|f|_y = |f|_{β(y)}` for `f ∈ R_a(𝒯)`, where on
the left `f` is a section of degree `(a, 0)` of `𝒴`. -/
theorem secAbs_steinBeta (y : A.model.an) {a : Fin 1 → ℤ} {f : A.FunField}
    (hf : f ∈ A.steinModel.sections a) :
    A.model.secAbs y.1 (steinDeg a) f = A.steinModel.secAbs (A.steinBeta y).1 a f := by
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := hf
  have hy : y = (FiniteHom.ofNormalization A.model).anMap (A.normHomeomorph.symm y) := by
    rw [← normHomeomorph_apply, Homeomorph.apply_symm_apply]
  have hb' := A.isAdmissible_normalization hb
  conv_lhs => rw [hy]
  rw [← (FiniteHom.ofNormalization A.model).secAbs_anMap_of_self
      A.isIntegrallyClosed_chartAlg_model _ hb'.mem_sections,
    secAbs_eq (A.normHomeomorph.symm y).2.2 hb', secAbs_eq (A.steinBeta y).2.2 hb, secAbsAt,
    secAbsAt]
  refine (A.sup_monSet_steinMon b _).trans (Finset.sup_congr rfl fun γ hγ => ?_)
  rw [A.homNorm_steinBeta y (hb.mul_zCoeff_mem hγ), addDeg_steinDeg,
    show A.model.normalization.zCoeff (A.steinMon γ) = A.steinModel.zCoeff γ from
      A.zCoeff_steinMon γ]

theorem logSecAbs_steinBeta (y : A.model.an) {a : Fin 1 → ℤ} {f : A.FunField}
    (hf : f ∈ A.steinModel.sections a) :
    A.model.logSecAbs y.1 (steinDeg a) f = A.steinModel.logSecAbs (A.steinBeta y).1 a f := by
  rw [logSecAbs, logSecAbs, A.secAbs_steinBeta y hf]

/-- Fubini–Study data of class `a` on `𝒯` as data of class `(a, 0)` on `𝒴`: the same `m`, sections
and constants, in degree `(m a, 0)`. -/
def steinFSData {a : Fin 1 → ℚ} (D : A.steinModel.FSData a) : A.model.FSData (steinDeg a) where
  m := D.m
  m_pos := D.m_pos
  deg := steinDeg D.deg
  deg_eq c := by
    refine Fin.cases ?_ (fun c => ?_) c <;> simp [steinDeg, D.deg_eq 0]
  terms := D.terms
  mem_sections t ht := A.mem_sections_stein (D.mem_sections t ht)

theorem eval_steinFSData {a : Fin 1 → ℚ} (D : A.steinModel.FSData a) (y : A.model.an) :
    (A.steinFSData D).eval y = D.eval (A.steinBeta y) := by
  rw [MultiModel.FSData.eval_def, MultiModel.FSData.eval_def]
  refine congrArg _ (Finset.sup_congr rfl fun t ht => ?_)
  change A.model.logSecAbs y.1 (steinDeg D.deg) t.1 + (t.2 : EReal) =
    A.steinModel.logSecAbs (A.steinBeta y).1 D.deg t.1 + (t.2 : EReal)
  rw [A.logSecAbs_steinBeta y (D.mem_sections t ht)]

/-- **Pullback of Fubini–Study functions** (`lem:gl-stein`(2)): `φ ∘ β ∈ 𝓗(𝒴, (a, 0))` for
`φ ∈ 𝓗(𝒯, a)`. -/
theorem isFS_comp_steinBeta {a : Fin 1 → ℚ} {φ : A.steinModel.an → EReal}
    (hφ : A.steinModel.IsFS a φ) : A.model.IsFS (steinDeg a) (φ ∘ A.steinBeta) := by
  obtain ⟨D, ⟨t, ht, ht0⟩, hD⟩ := hφ
  exact ⟨A.steinFSData D, ⟨t, ht, ht0⟩, fun y => by
    rw [Function.comp_apply, hD, eval_steinFSData]⟩

/-- **Pullback of psh functions** (`lem:gl-stein`(2)): `u ∘ β ∈ PSH(𝒴, (θ, 0))` for
`u ∈ PSH(𝒯, θ)` (pull back the decreasing nets of Fubini–Study functions). -/
theorem isPSH_comp_steinBeta {θ : Fin 1 → ℝ} {u : A.steinModel.an → EReal}
    (hu : A.steinModel.IsPSH θ u) : A.model.IsPSH (steinDeg θ) (u ∘ A.steinBeta) := by
  have hne := MultiModel.IsPSH.apply_triv_ne_bot hu
  obtain ⟨-, husc, ι, hpre, hdir, hnon, q, f, hf, hq, hanti, hinf⟩ := hu
  refine ⟨⟨A.model.triv, ?_⟩, husc.comp A.continuous_steinBeta, ι, hpre, hdir, hnon,
    fun i => steinDeg (q i), fun i => f i ∘ A.steinBeta, fun i => A.isFS_comp_steinBeta (hf i),
    ?_, fun y => hanti _, fun y => hinf _⟩
  · rw [Function.comp_apply, steinBeta_triv]
    exact hne
  · refine tendsto_pi_nhds.2 fun c => ?_
    refine Fin.cases ?_ (fun c => ?_) c
    · simpa [steinDeg] using tendsto_pi_nhds.1 hq 0
    · simp [steinDeg]

end Stein


/-! ### `lem:gl-stein`(3): `T'`, the blowup `B` and the homeomorphisms `τ`, `ϑ` -/

theorem steinE_pos {e : ℕ} (ha : ∀ c, 0 < (Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 1) e) c) : 0 < e := by
  simpa using ha 0

theorem steinVec_pos {e : ℕ} (ha : ∀ c, 0 < (Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 1) e) c) :
    ∀ c, 0 < biVeroneseVec e c :=
  biVeroneseVec_pos (steinE_pos ha)

/-- The degree `(a, b) ↦ a + b D` in `ℕ^1`. -/
def blowupDegHom (D : ℕ) : ℕ × ℕ →+ (Fin 1 →₀ ℕ) :=
  (Finsupp.singleAddHom (0 : Fin 1)).comp (AddMonoidHom.fst ℕ ℕ + D • AddMonoidHom.snd ℕ ℕ)

theorem blowupDegHom_apply (D : ℕ) (p : ℕ × ℕ) :
    blowupDegHom D p = Finsupp.single 0 (p.1 + D * p.2) := by
  simp [blowupDegHom]

section Blowup

variable [IsAlgClosed k]

/-! #### `τ : 𝒯^an ≃ₜ T'^an` -/

section Tau

variable {e : ℕ} (ha : ∀ c, 0 < (Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 1) e) c) {NT : ℕ}
  (P : DegOnePres (A.steinModel.veronese ha) NT)

/-- `T' = V(I_{T'}) ⊆ ℙ^{N_T}`, presenting the Veronese `(S_T)_{(e)}` (generated in degree `1`),
is projectively normal (`lem:gl-stein`(3)). -/
theorem isProjNormal_steinTarget : P.toProjSubvariety.IsProjNormal :=
  P.isProjNormal_toProjSubvariety_iff.2 (isNormal_veronese A.isNormal_steinModel)

/-- **`τ : 𝒯^an ≃ₜ T'^an`** (`lem:gl-stein`(3)): the Veronese homeomorphism followed by the bridge
of the presentation (`lem:gl-veronese`, `lem:gl-bridge-points`(1)). -/
def steinTau : A.steinModel.an ≃ₜ P.toProjSubvariety.an :=
  (A.steinModel.veroneseHomeomorph ha).trans P.anHomeomorph.symm

theorem steinTau_val (w : A.steinModel.an) (F : MvPolynomial (Fin (NT + 1)) k) :
    (A.steinTau ha P w).1.1.val F = w.1.val (A.steinModel.veroneseAlgHom ha (P.homS F)) := by
  rw [steinTau, Homeomorph.trans_apply, DegOnePres.anHomeomorph_symm_val]
  rfl

theorem steinTau_triv : A.steinTau ha P A.steinModel.triv = P.toProjSubvariety.triv := by
  rw [steinTau, Homeomorph.trans_apply, veroneseHomeomorph_triv,
    DegOnePres.anHomeomorph_symm_triv]

/-- **`PSH(𝒯, e t) = PSH(T', t) ∘ τ`** for `t ≥ 0` (`lem:gl-stein`(3); `lem:gl-veronese` and
`lem:gl-bridge-psh`(1)). -/
theorem isPSH_steinTau_iff {t : ℝ} (ht : 0 ≤ t) {u : P.toProjSubvariety.an → EReal} :
    P.toProjSubvariety.IsPSH t u ↔
      A.steinModel.IsPSH (fun _ => (e : ℝ) * t) (u ∘ A.steinTau ha P) := by
  have h1 := P.isPSH_comp_anHomeomorph_iff (A.isProjNormal_steinTarget ha P) ht
    (u := u ∘ P.anHomeomorph.symm)
  rw [Function.comp_assoc, Homeomorph.symm_comp_self, Function.comp_id] at h1
  rw [h1, isPSH_veronese_iff]
  have e1 : (fun c : Fin 1 => t * ((Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 1) e c : ℕ) : ℝ)) =
      fun _ => (e : ℝ) * t := by
    funext c
    obtain rfl := Fin.fin_one_eq_zero c
    simp [mul_comm]
  exact iff_of_eq (congrArg₂ _ e1 rfl)

end Tau

/-! #### The forms `G_m` and the blowup `B` -/

section Center

variable {e : ℕ} (ha : ∀ c, 0 < (Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 1) e) c)

include ha in
/-- **The forms `G_m`** (`lem:gl-stein`(3)): there are `D` and `0 ≠ h ∈ k(Y)` with
`g_m = (ȳ_m / ȳ_{m₀}) h ∈ (S_T)_{e D}` for all `m` (`k(T) = k(Y)`: a common denominator, then a
shift of degree by powers of the coordinate `x̄_{i₀} / x̄_{i₀} = 1`). -/
theorem exists_steinCenterData : ∃ (D : ℕ) (h : A.FunField), h ≠ 0 ∧
    ∀ m : Fin (A.N' + 1),
      A.yRatio m * h ∈ A.steinModel.piece (Finsupp.single 0 (D * e)) := by
  classical
  choose a f g hf hg hg0 hfg using fun m : Fin (A.N' + 1) =>
    A.steinModel.exists_eq_div (A.yRatio m)
  set h := ∏ m, g m
  set S := ∑ m, a m
  have hh0 : h ≠ 0 := Finset.prod_ne_zero_iff.2 fun m _ => hg0 m
  have hmem : ∀ m : Fin (A.N' + 1), A.yRatio m * h ∈ A.steinModel.piece S := by
    intro m
    have e1 : A.yRatio m * h = f m * ∏ m' ∈ Finset.univ.erase m, g m' := by
      rw [hfg m, show h = g m * ∏ m' ∈ Finset.univ.erase m, g m' from
        (Finset.mul_prod_erase Finset.univ g (Finset.mem_univ m)).symm]
      field_simp [hg0 m]
    have e2 : S = a m + ∑ m' ∈ Finset.univ.erase m, a m' :=
      (Finset.add_sum_erase _ _ (Finset.mem_univ m)).symm
    rw [e1, e2]
    exact mul_mem_piece (hf m) (prod_mem_piece _ fun m' _ => hg m')
  have he := steinE_pos ha
  have hone : (1 : A.FunField) ∈ A.steinModel.piece (Finsupp.single 0 1) := by
    have h1 : A.steinModel.coord 0 A.xIndex = 1 := quotCoord_self A.index A.isRelevantAt 0
    rw [← h1]
    exact A.steinModel.coord_mem_piece 0 A.xIndex
  refine ⟨S 0, h, hh0, fun m => ?_⟩
  have hdeg : S + (S 0 * e - S 0) • Finsupp.single 0 1 =
      Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 1) (S 0 * e) := by
    have hle : S 0 ≤ S 0 * e := Nat.le_mul_of_pos_right _ he
    refine Finsupp.ext fun c => ?_
    obtain rfl := Fin.fin_one_eq_zero c
    simp only [Finsupp.add_apply, Finsupp.smul_apply, Finsupp.single_eq_same, smul_eq_mul,
      mul_one]
    omega
  have := mul_mem_piece (hmem m) (pow_mem_piece hone (S 0 * e - S 0))
  rwa [one_pow, mul_one, hdeg] at this

variable {NT : ℕ} (P : DegOnePres (A.steinModel.veronese ha) NT) {D : ℕ} {h : A.FunField}
  (hh0 : h ≠ 0)
  (hmem : ∀ m : Fin (A.N' + 1),
    A.yRatio m * h ∈ A.steinModel.piece (Finsupp.single 0 (D * e)))

include hmem in
theorem mem_veronese_piece_steinCenter (m : Fin (A.N' + 1)) :
    A.yRatio m * h ∈ (A.steinModel.veronese ha).piece (Finsupp.single 0 D) := by
  rw [mem_veronese_piece_iff, Finsupp.smul_single, smul_eq_mul]
  exact hmem m

/-- **The blowup centre** `G_m` (`lem:gl-stein`(3)): forms of degree `D` on `T'` with
`G_m(w) = (ȳ_m / ȳ_{m₀}) h`, so that `ȳ_m / ȳ_{m₀} = G_m / G_{m₀}` in `k(Y)`. -/
def steinCenter : P.toProjSubvariety.BlowupCenter A.N' where
  d := D
  G m := P.form D (A.yRatio m * h)
  isHomogeneous _ := P.form_isHomogeneous D _
  exists_notMem := ⟨A.yIndex, fun hG => by
    have h1 := A.mem_veronese_piece_steinCenter ha hmem A.yIndex
    have h2 := (DegOnePres.mem_ideal_iff P).1 hG
    rw [P.hom_form h1, monomial_eq_zero, A.yRatio_yIndex, one_mul] at h2
    exact hh0 h2⟩

theorem hom_steinCenter_G (m : Fin (A.N' + 1)) :
    P.hom ((A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem).G m) =
      monomial (Finsupp.single 0 D) (A.yRatio m * h) :=
  P.hom_form (A.mem_veronese_piece_steinCenter ha hmem m)

end Center

/-! #### The model `𝒲` of the blowup inside `k(Y)` -/

section BlowupModel

variable {e : ℕ} (ha : ∀ c, 0 < (Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 1) e) c) {NT : ℕ}
  (P : DegOnePres (A.steinModel.veronese ha) NT)

/-- The coordinates of `𝒲`: `w_i` (the degree-`e` generators of `S_T`) in degree `e_1` and
`ȳ_m / ȳ_{m₀}` in degree `e_2`. -/
def blowupCoord : (c : Fin 2) → Fin (![NT, A.N'] c + 1) → A.FunField :=
  Fin.cons (α := fun c : Fin 2 => Fin (![NT, A.N'] c + 1) → A.FunField) P.w
    (Fin.cons (α := fun c : Fin 1 => Fin (![NT, A.N'] c.succ + 1) → A.FunField)
      A.yRatio fun i => i.elim0)

/-- The coordinate ring `k[w_i U_1, (ȳ_m / ȳ_{m₀}) U_2] ⊆ k(Y)[U_1, U_2]` of `𝒲`. -/
def blowupS : Subalgebra k (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A.FunField) :=
  Algebra.adjoin k (Set.range fun i : (Σ c : Fin 2, Fin (![NT, A.N'] c + 1)) =>
    (monomial (Finsupp.single i.1 1) (A.blowupCoord ha P i.1 i.2) :
      MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A.FunField))

/-- The subalgebra `k[w_i U_1]`. -/
def blowupBlock₀ : Subalgebra k (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A.FunField) :=
  Algebra.adjoin k (Set.range fun i : Fin (NT + 1) =>
    (monomial (Finsupp.single 0 1) (P.w i) : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A.FunField))

theorem blowupBlock₀_le : A.blowupBlock₀ ha P ≤ A.blowupS ha P :=
  Algebra.adjoin_le (Set.range_subset_iff.2 fun i => Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨⟨0, i⟩, rfl⟩)

theorem gen_mem_blowupS_one (m : Fin (A.N' + 1)) :
    (monomial (Finsupp.single 1 1) (A.yRatio m) :
      MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A.FunField) ∈ A.blowupS ha P :=
  Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨⟨1, m⟩, rfl⟩

/-- `T ↦ T_1` maps `(S_T)_{(e)} = k[w_i U]` into `k[w_i U_1]`. -/
theorem map_veronese_le_blowupBlock₀ :
    (A.steinModel.veronese ha).S.map (firstFactorHom k A.FunField) ≤ A.blowupBlock₀ ha P := by
  rw [← P.adjoin_eq, AlgHom.map_adjoin, Algebra.adjoin_le_iff]
  rintro _ ⟨_, ⟨i, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
  rw [firstFactorHom_monomial, firstDeg_single]
  exact Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨i, rfl⟩

omit [IsAlgClosed k] in
/-- A multi-index of degree `e_c` is a single coordinate. -/
theorem _root_.EnvelopeProperty.MultiModel.exists_eq_single_of_mem_monSet_single {r : ℕ}
    {K' : Type u} [Field K'] [Algebra k K'] {Y : MultiModel k K' r} {c : Fin r}
    {β : Y.CoordIndex →₀ ℕ} (hβ : β ∈ Y.monSet (Finsupp.single c 1)) :
    ∃ j : Fin (Y.M c + 1), β = Finsupp.single ⟨c, j⟩ 1 := by
  obtain ⟨j, γ, rfl, hγ⟩ := exists_eq_single_add_of_monDeg_eq (e := 0)
    (by rw [add_zero]; exact (Y.mem_monSet).1 hβ)
  rw [monDeg_eq_zero_iff] at hγ
  exact ⟨j, by rw [hγ, add_zero]⟩

/-- An `x`-monomial of degree `e` of `𝒴` lies in `k[w_i U_1]`. -/
theorem monomial_zCoeff_mem_blowupBlock₀ {β : A.model.CoordIndex →₀ ℕ}
    (hβ : β ∈ A.model.monSet (Finsupp.single 0 e)) :
    (monomial (Finsupp.single 0 1) (A.model.zCoeff β) : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A.FunField) ∈
      A.blowupBlock₀ ha P := by
  obtain ⟨γ, hγ, rfl⟩ := A.exists_steinMon_eq (b := Finsupp.single 0 e) (by rwa [firstDeg_single])
  rw [zCoeff_steinMon]
  have hp : A.steinModel.zCoeff γ ∈ (A.steinModel.veronese ha).piece (Finsupp.single 0 1) := by
    rw [mem_veronese_piece_iff, one_smul]
    exact zCoeff_mem_piece_of_mem_monSet hγ
  refine A.map_veronese_le_blowupBlock₀ ha P (Subalgebra.mem_map.2 ⟨_, hp, ?_⟩)
  rw [firstFactorHom_monomial, firstDeg_single]

/-- The generators of `k[z]_{(e,1) ℕ²}` lie in `S_𝒲`. -/
theorem multiVeroneseCoordAlg_le_blowupS :
    A.model.multiVeroneseCoordAlg (biVeroneseVec e) ≤ A.blowupS ha P := by
  refine Algebra.adjoin_le ?_
  rintro _ ⟨⟨c, j⟩, rfl⟩
  revert j
  refine Fin.cases (fun j => ?_) (fun c j => ?_) c
  · have hβ := (A.model.multiVeroneseEnum (biVeroneseVec e) 0 j).2
    exact A.blowupBlock₀_le ha P (A.monomial_zCoeff_mem_blowupBlock₀ ha P hβ)
  · obtain rfl := Fin.fin_one_eq_zero c
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := exists_eq_single_of_mem_monSet_single
      (A.model.multiVeroneseEnum (biVeroneseVec e) (Fin.succ 0) j).2
    change (monomial (Finsupp.single (Fin.succ 0) 1) (A.model.zCoeff
      (A.model.multiVeroneseEnum (biVeroneseVec e) (Fin.succ 0) j).1) :
        MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A.FunField) ∈ _
    rw [hm, zCoeff_single, pow_one]
    exact A.gen_mem_blowupS_one ha P m

/-- **`S_{(e,1)}(𝒴) ⊆ S_𝒲`** (`lem:gl-stein`(3): the image of the bigraded ring of `B` contains
the `(e, 1)`-Veronese of `S_Y`). -/
theorem multiVeroneseS_le_blowupS :
    A.model.multiVeroneseS (biVeroneseVec e) ≤ A.blowupS ha P := by
  intro p hp
  rw [p.as_sum]
  refine Subalgebra.sum_mem _ fun u _ => ?_
  have hu := isGraded_multiVeroneseS (steinVec_pos ha) hp u
  rw [monomial_mem_multiVeroneseS_iff] at hu
  have h1 := monomial_coeff_mem_multiVeroneseCoordAlg (a := biVeroneseVec e) (X := A.model)
    (P := monomial (biVeroneseVec e * u) (p.coeff u)) hu u
  rw [coeff_monomial, if_pos rfl] at h1
  exact A.multiVeroneseCoordAlg_le_blowupS ha P h1

/-- **`S_𝒲 ⊆ S_{(e,1)}(𝒴^ν)`** (`lem:gl-stein`(3): the image lies in the normalization of the
`(e, 1)`-Veronese). -/
theorem blowupS_le :
    A.blowupS ha P ≤ A.model.normalization.multiVeroneseS (biVeroneseVec e) := by
  refine Algebra.adjoin_le ?_
  rintro _ ⟨⟨c, j⟩, rfl⟩
  revert j
  refine Fin.cases (fun j => ?_) (fun c j => ?_) c
  · change monomial (Finsupp.single 0 1) (P.w j) ∈
      A.model.normalization.multiVeroneseS (biVeroneseVec e)
    rw [monomial_mem_multiVeroneseS_iff, mul_single_eq, mul_one, biVeroneseVec_zero]
    have hw : P.w j ∈ A.steinModel.piece (Finsupp.single 0 e) := by
      have := P.mem j
      rwa [mem_veronese_piece_iff, one_smul] at this
    change monomial (Finsupp.single 0 e) (P.w j) ∈ A.model.normalization.S
    rw [← firstDeg_single, ← firstFactorHom_monomial (k := k)]
    exact A.firstFactorHom_mem_normalization hw
  · obtain rfl := Fin.fin_one_eq_zero c
    change monomial (Finsupp.single (Fin.succ 0) 1) (quotCoord A.ideal A.index 1 j) ∈
      A.model.normalization.multiVeroneseS (biVeroneseVec e)
    rw [monomial_mem_multiVeroneseS_iff, mul_single_eq, mul_one]
    exact A.model.le_normalization_S (A.model.coord_mem 1 j)

/-- **The model `𝒲`** (`lem:gl-stein`(3)): `k[w_i U_1, (ȳ_m / ȳ_{m₀}) U_2] ⊆ k(Y)[U_1, U_2]` with
coordinates `w_i`, `ȳ_m / ȳ_{m₀}`; the image of the bigraded ring of the blowup `B`. -/
def blowupModel : MultiModel k A.FunField 2 where
  S := A.blowupS ha P
  isGraded _ hp a := monomial_coeff_mem_adjoin (fun q hq => by
    obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := hq
    exact ⟨_, _, rfl⟩) hp a
  fg := ⟨(Set.finite_range _).toFinset, by rw [Set.Finite.coe_toFinset]; rfl⟩
  M := ![NT, A.N']
  coord := A.blowupCoord ha P
  coord_mem c j := Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨⟨c, j⟩, rfl⟩
  exists_coord_ne_zero c := by
    refine Fin.cases ?_ (fun c => ?_) c
    · exact P.exists_w_ne_zero
    · obtain rfl := Fin.fin_one_eq_zero c
      refine ⟨A.yIndex, ?_⟩
      change A.yRatio A.yIndex ≠ 0
      rw [A.yRatio_yIndex]
      exact one_ne_zero
  isIntegral p hp := isIntegral_algebraMap (R := A.blowupS ha P) (x := ⟨p, hp⟩)
  generates := by
    rw [eq_top_iff, ← A.model.generates_multiVeroneseS (steinVec_pos ha),
      IntermediateField.adjoin_le_iff]
    rintro x ⟨u, f, g, hf, hg, hg0, rfl⟩
    exact IntermediateField.subset_adjoin _ _ ⟨u, f, g, A.multiVeroneseS_le_blowupS ha P hf,
      A.multiVeroneseS_le_blowupS ha P hg, hg0, rfl⟩

theorem blowupModel_S : (A.blowupModel ha P).S = (A.blowupModel ha P).coordAlg :=
  rfl

theorem blowupModel_M : (A.blowupModel ha P).M = ![NT, A.N'] :=
  rfl

/-! #### Change of model `𝒴_{(e,1)} ⊆ 𝒲 ⊆ (𝒴^ν)_{(e,1)}` -/

/-- The coordinates of `𝒲` of degree `e_c` are integral over those of `𝒴_{(e,1)}`. -/
theorem blowupCoord_isIntegral (c : Fin 2) (j : Fin ((A.blowupModel ha P).M c + 1)) :
    IsIntegral ((A.model.biVeronese (steinE_pos ha)).blockAlg c)
      (monomial (Finsupp.single c 1) ((A.blowupModel ha P).coord c j)) := by
  revert j
  refine Fin.cases (fun j => ?_) (fun c j => ?_) c
  · -- `w_j T^e ∈ S_T` is integral over the `x`-monomials of degree `e`
    have hw : P.w j ∈ A.steinModel.piece (1 • Finsupp.single 0 e) := by
      have := P.mem j
      rwa [mem_veronese_piece_iff] at this
    have hint := isIntegral_segreAlg_monomial (X := A.steinModel) (a := Finsupp.single 0 e) hw
    have hle : (A.steinModel.segreAlg (Finsupp.single 0 e)).map (firstFactorHom k A.FunField) ≤
        (A.model.biVeronese (steinE_pos ha)).blockAlg 0 := by
      rw [segreAlg, AlgHom.map_adjoin, Algebra.adjoin_le_iff]
      rintro _ ⟨_, ⟨β, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
      have hβ := A.steinMon_mem_monSet β.2
      rw [firstDeg_single] at hβ
      refine Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨(A.model.multiVeroneseEnum (biVeroneseVec e) 0).symm
        ⟨A.steinMon β.1, hβ⟩, ?_⟩
      change monomial (Finsupp.single 0 1) (A.model.zCoeff ((A.model.multiVeroneseEnum
        (biVeroneseVec e) 0) ((A.model.multiVeroneseEnum (biVeroneseVec e) 0).symm
          ⟨A.steinMon β.1, hβ⟩)).1) = _
      rw [Equiv.apply_symm_apply, zCoeff_steinMon, firstFactorHom_monomial, firstDeg_single]
    let φ : A.steinModel.segreAlg (Finsupp.single 0 e) →+*
        (A.model.biVeronese (steinE_pos ha)).blockAlg 0 :=
      ((firstFactorHom k A.FunField).toRingHom.comp
        (A.steinModel.segreAlg (Finsupp.single 0 e)).val.toRingHom).codRestrict _
        fun q => hle (Subalgebra.mem_map.2 ⟨q.1, q.2, rfl⟩)
    have := IsIntegral.map_of_comp_eq φ (firstFactorHom k A.FunField).toRingHom
      (RingHom.ext fun _ => rfl) hint
    change IsIntegral _ (monomial (Finsupp.single 0 1) (P.w j))
    rwa [AlgHom.toRingHom_eq_coe, RingHom.coe_coe, firstFactorHom_monomial,
      firstDeg_single] at this
  · obtain rfl := Fin.fin_one_eq_zero c
    have hβ : (Finsupp.single (⟨Fin.succ 0, j⟩ : A.model.CoordIndex) 1) ∈
        A.model.monSet (Finsupp.single (Fin.succ 0) (biVeroneseVec e (Fin.succ 0))) := by
      rw [mem_monSet, monDeg_single]
      rfl
    have hmem : (monomial (Finsupp.single (Fin.succ 0) 1)
        ((A.blowupModel ha P).coord (Fin.succ 0) j) : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A.FunField) ∈
          (A.model.biVeronese (steinE_pos ha)).blockAlg (Fin.succ 0) := by
      refine Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨(A.model.multiVeroneseEnum (biVeroneseVec e)
        (Fin.succ 0)).symm ⟨_, hβ⟩, ?_⟩
      change monomial (Finsupp.single (Fin.succ 0) 1) (A.model.zCoeff
        ((A.model.multiVeroneseEnum (biVeroneseVec e) (Fin.succ 0))
          ((A.model.multiVeroneseEnum (biVeroneseVec e) (Fin.succ 0)).symm ⟨_, hβ⟩)).1) = _
      rw [Equiv.apply_symm_apply, zCoeff_single, pow_one]
      rfl
    exact isIntegral_algebraMap (x := (⟨_, hmem⟩ :
      (A.model.biVeronese (steinE_pos ha)).blockAlg (Fin.succ 0)))

/-- The coordinates of `𝒴_{(e,1)}` of degree `e_c` lie in the subalgebra generated by those of
`𝒲`. -/
theorem multiVeroneseCoord_isIntegral_blowup (c : Fin 2)
    (j : Fin ((A.model.biVeronese (steinE_pos ha)).M c + 1)) :
    IsIntegral ((A.blowupModel ha P).blockAlg c)
      (monomial (Finsupp.single c 1) ((A.model.biVeronese (steinE_pos ha)).coord c j)) := by
  revert j
  refine Fin.cases (fun j => ?_) (fun c j => ?_) c
  · have hβ := (A.model.multiVeroneseEnum (biVeroneseVec e) 0 j).2
    have hmem : (monomial (Finsupp.single 0 1) ((A.model.biVeronese (steinE_pos ha)).coord 0 j) :
        MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A.FunField) ∈ (A.blowupModel ha P).blockAlg 0 :=
      A.monomial_zCoeff_mem_blowupBlock₀ ha P hβ
    exact isIntegral_algebraMap (x := (⟨_, hmem⟩ : (A.blowupModel ha P).blockAlg 0))
  · obtain rfl := Fin.fin_one_eq_zero c
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := exists_eq_single_of_mem_monSet_single
      (A.model.multiVeroneseEnum (biVeroneseVec e) (Fin.succ 0) j).2
    have hmem : (monomial (Finsupp.single (Fin.succ 0) 1)
        ((A.model.biVeronese (steinE_pos ha)).coord (Fin.succ 0) j) :
          MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A.FunField) ∈ (A.blowupModel ha P).blockAlg (Fin.succ 0) := by
      change monomial (Finsupp.single (Fin.succ 0) 1) (A.model.zCoeff
        (A.model.multiVeroneseEnum (biVeroneseVec e) (Fin.succ 0) j).1) ∈ _
      rw [hm, zCoeff_single, pow_one]
      exact Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨m, rfl⟩
    exact isIntegral_algebraMap (x := (⟨_, hmem⟩ : (A.blowupModel ha P).blockAlg (Fin.succ 0)))

/-- **Change of model** `𝒴_{(e,1)} ⊆ 𝒲` (`lem:gl-model-change`). -/
theorem isModelChange_blowupModel :
    IsModelChange (A.model.biVeronese (steinE_pos ha)) (A.blowupModel ha P) where
  le := A.multiVeroneseS_le_blowupS ha P
  isIntegral _ hp := isIntegral_multiVeroneseS_of_mem_normalization (steinVec_pos ha)
    (A.blowupS_le ha P hp)
  coord_isIntegral := A.blowupCoord_isIntegral ha P
  coord_isIntegral' := A.multiVeroneseCoord_isIntegral_blowup ha P

/-- **Change of model** `𝒲 ⊆ (𝒴^ν)_{(e,1)}`. -/
theorem isModelChange_blowupModel_normalization :
    IsModelChange (A.blowupModel ha P) (A.model.normalization.biVeronese (steinE_pos ha)) where
  le := A.blowupS_le ha P
  isIntegral _ hp := isIntegral_of_le_subalgebra (A.multiVeroneseS_le_blowupS ha P)
    (isIntegral_multiVeroneseS_of_mem_normalization (steinVec_pos ha) hp)
  coord_isIntegral c j := A.multiVeroneseCoord_isIntegral_blowup ha P c j
  coord_isIntegral' c j := A.blowupCoord_isIntegral ha P c j

/-- The elements of `S_𝒲` are sections of `𝒴_{(e,1)}` (the ideal argument on the smooth `𝒴`). -/
theorem hasSections_blowupModel :
    IsModelChange.HasSections (A.model.biVeronese (steinE_pos ha)) (A.blowupModel ha P) :=
  hasSections_multiVeronese (steinVec_pos ha) A.isIntegrallyClosed_chartAlg_model
    fun u f hf => by
      have := A.blowupS_le ha P hf
      rw [monomial_mem_multiVeroneseS_iff] at this
      exact mem_normalization_S.1 (mem_piece.1 this)

/-- **`𝒴^an ≃ₜ 𝒲^an`**: the `(e, 1)`-Veronese homeomorphism followed by the change of model. -/
def blowupHomeomorph : A.model.an ≃ₜ (A.blowupModel ha P).an :=
  (A.model.multiVeroneseHomeomorph (steinVec_pos ha)).trans
    ((A.isModelChange_blowupModel ha P).restrictHomeomorph (A.hasSections_blowupModel ha P)).symm

theorem blowupHomeomorph_triv : A.blowupHomeomorph ha P A.model.triv = (A.blowupModel ha P).triv := by
  rw [blowupHomeomorph, Homeomorph.trans_apply, multiVeroneseHomeomorph_triv,
    Homeomorph.symm_apply_eq, IsModelChange.restrictHomeomorph_apply,
    IsModelChange.restrictAn_triv]

/-- **The value formula**: `|q|_{ϑ_𝒲(y)} = |ψ(q)|_{ỹ}` for `q ∈ S_𝒲`, `ψ : U_1 ↦ T_1^e, U_2 ↦ T_2`,
`ỹ` the extension of `y` to `S_Y^ν`. -/
theorem blowupHomeomorph_val (y : A.model.an) (q : (A.blowupModel ha P).S) :
    (A.blowupHomeomorph ha P y).1.val q = (A.normHomeomorph.symm y).1.val
      (A.model.normalization.multiVeroneseAlgHom (steinVec_pos ha)
        ((A.isModelChange_blowupModel_normalization ha P).inclHom q)) := by
  set h₁ := A.isModelChange_blowupModel ha P
  set h₂ := A.isModelChange_blowupModel_normalization ha P
  set hR := A.hasSections_blowupModel ha P
  have hy : y = (FiniteHom.ofNormalization A.model).anMap (A.normHomeomorph.symm y) := by
    rw [← normHomeomorph_apply, Homeomorph.apply_symm_apply]
  set z := h₂.restrictAn (A.model.normalization.multiVeroneseAnMap (steinVec_pos ha)
    (A.normHomeomorph.symm y))
  have hz : A.blowupHomeomorph ha P y = z := by
    apply h₁.restrictAn_injective hR
    have e1 : h₁.restrictAn (A.blowupHomeomorph ha P y) =
        A.model.multiVeroneseAnMap (steinVec_pos ha) y := by
      change h₁.restrictHomeomorph hR ((h₁.restrictHomeomorph hR).symm _) = _
      rw [Homeomorph.apply_symm_apply]
      rfl
    rw [e1]
    refine Subtype.ext (Berk.ext_val fun p => ?_)
    rw [multiVeroneseAnMap_val, IsModelChange.restrictAn_val, IsModelChange.restrictAn_val,
      multiVeroneseAnMap_val]
    conv_lhs => rw [hy]
    rw [FiniteHom.anMap_val]
    refine congrArg (A.normHomeomorph.symm y).1.val (Subtype.ext ?_)
    rw [FiniteHom.coe_algHom, FiniteHom.coeffMap_self, coe_multiVeroneseAlgHom,
      coe_multiVeroneseAlgHom, IsModelChange.coe_inclHom, IsModelChange.coe_inclHom]
  rw [hz, IsModelChange.restrictAn_val, multiVeroneseAnMap_val]

/-! #### The kernel of the presentation of `𝒲` is the ideal of the blowup -/

variable {D : ℕ} {h : A.FunField} (hh0 : h ≠ 0)
  (hmem : ∀ m : Fin (A.N' + 1),
    A.yRatio m * h ∈ A.steinModel.piece (Finsupp.single 0 (D * e)))

/-- For bihomogeneous `F`: `F ∈ ker(k[x', y] → S_𝒲)` iff `F ∈ I'` (`lem:gl-stein`(3), proof:
`F(x', G) = h^b F(w, ȳ / ȳ_{m₀})` for `F` of bidegree `(a, b)`, `lem:pg-blowup-basic`(1)). -/
theorem mem_blowupModel_biIdeal_iff {p : ℕ × ℕ}
    {F : MvPolynomial (Fin (NT + 1) ⊕ Fin (A.N' + 1)) k}
    (hF : F.IsWeightedHomogeneous (biWeight NT A.N') p) :
    F ∈ (A.blowupModel ha P).biIdeal ↔ F ∈ (A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem).ideal := by
  obtain ⟨a, b⟩ := p
  have hW : (A.blowupModel ha P).biHom F =
      monomial (biDeg (a, b)) (aeval (A.blowupModel ha P).biCoeff F) :=
    aeval_monomial_family_of_isWeightedHomogeneous biDeg (biWeight _ _) _ hF
  have hcomp : P.hom ((A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem).subst F) =
      aeval (fun v => (monomial (blowupDegHom D (biWeight NT A.N' v))
        (Sum.elim P.w (fun m => A.yRatio m * h) v) :
          MvPolynomial (Fin 1) A.FunField)) F := by
    rw [BlowupCenter.subst, comp_aeval_apply]
    refine congrArg (fun φ => aeval φ F) (funext fun v => ?_)
    rcases v with i | m
    · rw [Sum.elim_inl, Sum.elim_inl, biWeight_inl, blowupDegHom_apply, DegOnePres.hom_X]
      simp [DegOnePres.gen]
    · rw [Sum.elim_inr, Sum.elim_inr, biWeight_inr, blowupDegHom_apply,
        A.hom_steinCenter_G ha P hh0 hmem m]
      simp
  have hB : P.hom ((A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem).subst F) =
      monomial (blowupDegHom D (a, b))
        (aeval (Sum.elim P.w fun m => A.yRatio m * h) F) :=
    hcomp.trans (aeval_monomial_family_of_isWeightedHomogeneous _ _ _ hF)
  have hscale : aeval (Sum.elim P.w fun m => A.yRatio m * h) F =
      h ^ b * aeval (Sum.elim P.w A.yRatio) F := by
    have := hF.aeval_pow_mul_pow_mul (1 : A.FunField) h
      (Sum.elim P.w A.yRatio)
    rw [one_pow, one_mul] at this
    rw [← this]
    refine congrArg (fun φ => aeval φ F) (funext fun v => ?_)
    rcases v with i | m
    · simp
    · simp [mul_comm]
  have step1 : F ∈ (A.blowupModel ha P).biIdeal ↔
      aeval (A.blowupModel ha P).biCoeff F = 0 := by
    have : F ∈ (A.blowupModel ha P).biIdeal ↔ (A.blowupModel ha P).biHom F = 0 :=
      ((A.blowupModel ha P).mem_biIdeal_iff).trans ⟨fun h0 => congrArg Subtype.val h0, fun h0 => Subtype.ext h0⟩
    rw [this, hW, monomial_eq_zero]
  have step2 : F ∈ (A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem).ideal ↔
      aeval (Sum.elim P.w A.yRatio) F = 0 := by
    rw [BlowupCenter.mem_ideal_iff_of_isWeightedHomogeneous _ hF,
      DegOnePres.toProjSubvariety_ideal, DegOnePres.mem_ideal_iff, hB, monomial_eq_zero, hscale,
      mul_eq_zero, or_iff_right (pow_ne_zero _ hh0)]
  exact step1.trans step2.symm

/-- **The kernel of `k[x', y] → S_𝒲` is the ideal `I'` of the blowup `B` of `T'` along `(G_m)`**
(`lem:gl-stein`(3)). -/
theorem blowupModel_biIdeal :
    (A.blowupModel ha P).biIdeal = (A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem).ideal := by
  ext F
  constructor
  · intro hF
    refine (A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem).mem_ideal_iff.2 fun p => ?_
    have h1 := (A.blowupModel ha P).weightedHomogeneousComponent_mem_biIdeal hF p
    have h2 := (A.mem_blowupModel_biIdeal_iff ha P hh0 hmem
      (weightedHomogeneousComponent_isWeightedHomogeneous p F)).1 h1
    exact ((A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem).mem_ideal_iff_of_isWeightedHomogeneous
      (weightedHomogeneousComponent_isWeightedHomogeneous p F)).1 h2
  · intro hF
    rw [← sum_weightSupport (w := biWeight NT A.N') F]
    refine Ideal.sum_mem _ fun p _ => ?_
    exact (A.mem_blowupModel_biIdeal_iff ha P hh0 hmem
      (weightedHomogeneousComponent_isWeightedHomogeneous p F)).2
      ((A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem).weightedHomogeneousComponent_mem_ideal hF p)

/-! #### `ϑ : 𝒴^an ≃ₜ B^an` -/

/-- **`ϑ : 𝒴^an ≃ₜ B^an`** (`lem:gl-stein`(3)): `𝒴^an ≃ 𝒴_{(e,1)}^an ≃ 𝒲^an ≃ B^an`
(`lem:gl-veronese` with the rescaling `(e, 1)`, `lem:gl-model-change`, `lem:gl-bridge-points`(2)). -/
def steinTheta : A.model.an ≃ₜ (A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem).an :=
  (A.blowupHomeomorph ha P).trans (blowupAnHomeomorph (A.blowupModel_S ha P)
    (A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem) (A.blowupModel_biIdeal ha P hh0 hmem))

theorem steinTheta_triv :
    A.steinTheta ha P hh0 hmem A.model.triv = (A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem).triv := by
  classical
  refine Subtype.ext (Subtype.ext (Berk.ext_val fun F => ?_))
  refine (blowupAnHomeomorph_val (A.blowupModel_S ha P) (A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem)
    (A.blowupModel_biIdeal ha P hh0 hmem) (A.blowupHomeomorph ha P A.model.triv) F).trans ?_
  rw [A.blowupHomeomorph_triv ha P]
  by_cases hF : F ∈ (A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem).ideal
  · rw [BlowupCenter.triv_val_of_mem _ hF]
    have h0 : (A.blowupModel ha P).biHomS F = 0 :=
      (A.blowupModel ha P).mem_biIdeal_iff.1 ((SetLike.ext_iff.1 (A.blowupModel_biIdeal ha P hh0 hmem) F).2 hF)
    rw [h0, map_zero]
  · rw [BlowupCenter.triv_val_of_notMem _ hF]
    have h0 : (A.blowupModel ha P).biHomS F ≠ 0 := fun h0 =>
      hF ((SetLike.ext_iff.1 (A.blowupModel_biIdeal ha P hh0 hmem) F).1 ((A.blowupModel ha P).mem_biIdeal_iff.2 h0))
    exact (A.blowupModel ha P).triv_val_of_ne_zero h0

/-- `x_i ↦ w_i U_1 ↦ w_i T_1^e` is `x_i ↦ w_i U ↦ w_i T^e ↦ w_i T_1^e`. -/
theorem multiVeroneseHom_comp_biHom (F : MvPolynomial (Fin ((A.blowupModel ha P).M 0 + 1)) k) :
    multiVeroneseHom k (biVeroneseVec e) ((A.blowupModel ha P).biHom (rename Sum.inl F)) =
      firstFactorHom k A.FunField (veroneseHom k (Finsupp.single 0 e) (P.hom F)) := by
  have key : ((multiVeroneseHom k (biVeroneseVec e)).comp ((A.blowupModel ha P).biHom.comp
      (rename Sum.inl))) =
      (firstFactorHom k A.FunField).comp ((veroneseHom k (Finsupp.single 0 e)).comp P.hom) := by
    refine MvPolynomial.algHom_ext fun i => ?_
    have l1 : (A.blowupModel ha P).biHom (rename Sum.inl (MvPolynomial.X i)) =
        monomial (Finsupp.single 0 1) (P.w i) := by
      rw [rename_X, biHom_X_inl]
      rfl
    have lhs : multiVeroneseHom k (biVeroneseVec e)
        ((A.blowupModel ha P).biHom (rename Sum.inl (MvPolynomial.X i))) =
          monomial (Finsupp.single 0 e) (P.w i) := by
      rw [l1, multiVeroneseHom_monomial, mul_single_eq, mul_one, biVeroneseVec_zero]
    have rhs : ∀ j : Fin (NT + 1), firstFactorHom k A.FunField (veroneseHom k
        (Finsupp.single 0 e) (P.hom (MvPolynomial.X j))) = monomial (Finsupp.single 0 e) (P.w j) := by
      intro j
      rw [DegOnePres.hom_X, DegOnePres.gen, veroneseHom_monomial_single, one_smul,
        firstFactorHom_monomial, firstDeg_single]
    exact lhs.trans (rhs i).symm
  exact DFunLike.congr_fun key F

/-- **`μ ∘ ϑ = τ ∘ β`** (`lem:gl-stein`(3)): both send `y` to the point
`F ↦ |F(w T_1^e)|_{ỹ}` of `T'^an`. -/
theorem proj_steinTheta (y : A.model.an) :
    (A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem).proj (A.steinTheta ha P hh0 hmem y) =
      A.steinTau ha P (A.steinBeta y) := by
  refine Subtype.ext (Subtype.ext (Berk.ext_val fun F => ?_))
  change ((A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem).proj (blowupAnHomeomorph (A.blowupModel_S ha P)
    (A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem) (A.blowupModel_biIdeal ha P hh0 hmem)
      (A.blowupHomeomorph ha P y)) : ProjBerk k NT).1.val F =
    (A.steinTau ha P (A.steinBeta y)).1.1.val F
  refine (proj_blowupAnHomeomorph_val (A.blowupModel_S ha P) (A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem)
    (A.blowupModel_biIdeal ha P hh0 hmem) (A.blowupHomeomorph ha P y) F).trans ?_
  rw [steinTau_val, A.blowupHomeomorph_val, steinBeta_val]
  refine congrArg (A.normHomeomorph.symm y).1.val (Subtype.ext ?_)
  rw [coe_multiVeroneseAlgHom, IsModelChange.coe_inclHom, coe_biHomS, coe_steinRingHom,
    coe_veroneseAlgHom, DegOnePres.coe_homS]
  exact A.multiVeroneseHom_comp_biHom ha P F

/-- **`PSH(𝒴, (e t, s)) = PSH(B, (t, s)) ∘ ϑ`** for `t, s ≥ 0` (`lem:gl-stein`(3);
`lem:gl-veronese` with the rescaling `(e, 1)`, `lem:gl-model-change`, `lem:gl-bridge-psh`(2)). -/
theorem isPSH_steinTheta_iff {t s : ℝ} (ht : 0 ≤ t) (hs : 0 ≤ s)
    {u : (A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem).an → EReal} :
    (A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem).IsPSH ![t, s] u ↔
      A.model.IsPSH ![(e : ℝ) * t, s] (u ∘ A.steinTheta ha P hh0 hmem) := by
  have hθ : (0 : Fin 2 → ℝ) ≤ ![t, s] := fun c => by
    refine Fin.cases ?_ (fun c => ?_) c
    · simpa using ht
    · obtain rfl := Fin.fin_one_eq_zero c
      simpa using hs
  set bl := blowupAnHomeomorph (A.blowupModel_S ha P) (A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem)
    (A.blowupModel_biIdeal ha P hh0 hmem)
  set h₁ := A.isModelChange_blowupModel ha P
  set hR := A.hasSections_blowupModel ha P
  have e1 := (isPSH_comp_blowupAnHomeomorph_iff (A.blowupModel_S ha P)
    (A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem) (A.blowupModel_biIdeal ha P hh0 hmem) hθ (u := u)).symm
  have e2 : (A.blowupModel ha P).IsPSH ![t, s] (u ∘ bl) ↔
      (A.model.biVeronese (steinE_pos ha)).IsPSH ![t, s]
        (u ∘ bl ∘ (h₁.restrictHomeomorph hR).symm) := by
    have hc : (u ∘ bl ∘ (h₁.restrictHomeomorph hR).symm) ∘ h₁.restrictAn = u ∘ bl :=
      funext fun w => congrArg (u ∘ bl) ((h₁.restrictHomeomorph hR).symm_apply_apply w)
    have := h₁.isPSH_comp_iff hR (θ := ![t, s]) (u := u ∘ bl ∘ (h₁.restrictHomeomorph hR).symm)
    rw [hc] at this
    exact this
  have e3 := isPSH_biVeronese_iff A.model (steinE_pos ha) (t := t) (s := s)
    (u := u ∘ bl ∘ (h₁.restrictHomeomorph hR).symm)
  exact e1.trans (e2.trans e3)

end BlowupModel

/-! #### The data of `lem:gl-stein`(3) -/

/-- **The data of `lem:gl-stein`(3)**: `e ≥ 1`, a projectively normal `T' = V(I_{T'}) ⊆ ℙ^{N_T}`
presenting the Veronese `(S_T)_{(e)}`, the blowup `B` of `T'` along forms `G_0, …, G_{N'}` of one
degree with `ȳ_m / ȳ_{m₀} = G_m / G_{m₀}`, and homeomorphisms `τ : 𝒯^an ≃ₜ T'^an`,
`ϑ : 𝒴^an ≃ₜ B^an` preserving `⋆`, with `μ ∘ ϑ = τ ∘ β`,
`PSH(𝒯, e t) = PSH(T', t) ∘ τ` and `PSH(𝒴, (e t, s)) = PSH(B, (t, s)) ∘ ϑ` for `t, s ≥ 0`. -/
structure SteinBlowup where
  /-- The Veronese degree `e`. -/
  e : ℕ
  e_pos : 0 < e
  /-- `T' ⊆ ℙ^{N_T}`. -/
  NT : ℕ
  /-- The projectively normal `T'` presenting `(S_T)_{(e)}`. -/
  target : ProjSubvariety k NT
  isProjNormal : target.IsProjNormal
  /-- The centre `G_0, …, G_{N'}` of the blowup `B → T'`. -/
  center : target.BlowupCenter A.N'
  /-- `τ : 𝒯^an ≃ₜ T'^an`. -/
  tau : A.steinModel.an ≃ₜ target.an
  /-- `ϑ : 𝒴^an ≃ₜ B^an`. -/
  theta : A.model.an ≃ₜ center.an
  tau_triv : tau A.steinModel.triv = target.triv
  theta_triv : theta A.model.triv = center.triv
  /-- `μ ∘ ϑ = τ ∘ β`. -/
  proj_theta : ∀ y, center.proj (theta y) = tau (A.steinBeta y)
  /-- `PSH(𝒯, e t) = PSH(T', t) ∘ τ` for `t ≥ 0`. -/
  isPSH_tau_iff : ∀ {t : ℝ}, 0 ≤ t → ∀ u : target.an → EReal,
    target.IsPSH t u ↔ A.steinModel.IsPSH (fun _ => (e : ℝ) * t) (u ∘ tau)
  /-- `PSH(𝒴, (e t, s)) = PSH(B, (t, s)) ∘ ϑ` for `t, s ≥ 0`. -/
  isPSH_theta_iff : ∀ {t s : ℝ}, 0 ≤ t → 0 ≤ s → ∀ u : center.an → EReal,
    center.IsPSH ![t, s] u ↔ A.model.IsPSH ![(e : ℝ) * t, s] (u ∘ theta)

/-- **`lem:gl-stein`(3)**: the data exist. -/
theorem nonempty_steinBlowup : Nonempty A.SteinBlowup := by
  obtain ⟨e, ha, NT, ⟨P⟩⟩ := exists_degOnePres_veronese A.steinModel
  obtain ⟨D, h, hh0, hmem⟩ := A.exists_steinCenterData ha
  exact ⟨⟨e, steinE_pos ha, NT, P.toProjSubvariety, A.isProjNormal_steinTarget ha P,
    A.steinCenter ha P hh0 hmem, A.steinTau ha P, A.steinTheta ha P hh0 hmem,
    A.steinTau_triv ha P, A.steinTheta_triv ha P hh0 hmem, A.proj_steinTheta ha P hh0 hmem,
    fun ht _ => A.isPSH_steinTau_iff ha P ht,
    fun ht hs _ => A.isPSH_steinTheta_iff ha P hh0 hmem ht hs⟩⟩

/-- **`β` is surjective** (`lem:gl-stein`(2)): `β = τ⁻¹ ∘ μ ∘ ϑ` and the blowup map `μ` is
surjective (`lem:pg-blowup-surjective`). -/
theorem steinBeta_surjective : Function.Surjective A.steinBeta := by
  obtain ⟨S⟩ := A.nonempty_steinBlowup
  intro w
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := S.center.proj_surjective (S.tau w)
  refine ⟨S.theta.symm b, S.tau.injective ?_⟩
  rw [← S.proj_theta, Homeomorph.apply_symm_apply, hb]

end Blowup

end ProjSubvariety.Alteration

end EnvelopeProperty
